WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.533
Once a week it's worth stopping to decide what you're actually working on, instead of playing whatever comes to hand.

2
00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:16.300
This is your week: a short list of tunes to come back to over the next few days. It's empty because we haven't picked anything yet.

3
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.333
Underneath are four ways into your library, so you're not staring at all of it at once.

4
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:29.367
"To work on" is the tunes you flagged the last time you practiced them. (You flag this by picking "Work on this" when you practice a tune.)

5
00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:34.400
"Haven't played in a while" are tunes in your Repertoire that you haven't played in a while.

6
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.567
"Don't know yet" are tunes in your library that you aren't comfortable with yet.

7
00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.533
Or you can just pick from everything.

8
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:48.333
Let's look at the tunes in "To work on".

9
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:54.900
Each one comes with the note you left when you flagged it, so you can see what you were going to fix.

10
00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:08.933
Tap the ones you want. They go straight on This Week.

11
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:14.600
There they are. Two or three is plenty for a week.

12
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:27.067
The list isn't a schedule, and nothing's going to nag you about it. It's just a list you can go back to the next time that you sit down to play.

13
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:33.100
Which is here — "This Week", in with the other ways into your library. Pick one and away you go.
